{"entries":[{"id":"scofield-1ch-1-5","title":"1 Chronicles 1:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":1,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":1,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>Book Introduction - 1 Chronicles Read first chapter of 1 Chronicles The two books of Chronicles (like the two books of Kings) are but one book in the Jewish canon. Together they cover the period from the death of Saul to the captivities. They were written probably during the Babylonian captivity, and are distinguished from the two books of the Kings in a fuller account of Judah, and in the omission of many details. The blessing of God's earthly people in connection with the Davidic monarchy is probably the typical significance of these books. First Chronicles is in three parts: Official genealogies, 1:1-9:44. From the death of Saul to the accession of David, 10:1-12:24. From the accession of David to his death, 13:1-29:30. Excluding the genealogies (Ch 1-9) the events recorded in First Chronicles cover a period of 41 years (Ussher). Magog Genesis 10:2; Ezekiel 38:2; 39:6; Revelation 20:8. (See Scofield \"Ezekiel 38:2\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-2-13","title":"1 Chronicles 2:13","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>Shimma Or, Shammah, 1 Samuel 16:9.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-2-54","title":"1 Chronicles 2:54","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":2,"verseStart":54,"chapterEnd":2,"verseEnd":54},"content":"<p>Ataroth Or, Atarites, or, crowns of the house of Joab.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-3-2","title":"1 Chronicles 3:2","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":3,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":3,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Absalom (See Scofield \"2 Samuel 13:37\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-5-6","title":"1 Chronicles 5:6","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Tilgathpilneser Or, Tiglathpileser, 2 Kings 15:29; 16:7.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-5-20","title":"1 Chronicles 5:20","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>trust (See Scofield \"Psalms 2:12\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-6-68","title":"1 Chronicles 6:68","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":68,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":68},"content":"<p>Jokmeam See Joshua 21:22-35 where many of these cities have other names:</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-7-12","title":"1 Chronicles 7:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Shuppim Shupham and Hupham. Numbers 26:39.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-7-28","title":"1 Chronicles 7:28","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":7,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":7,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>Narran Naarath, Joshua 16:7.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-9-26","title":"1 Chronicles 9:26","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>chambers i.e. storehouses.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-9-32","title":"1 Chronicles 9:32","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>shewbread (See Scofield \"Exodus 25:30\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-9-41","title":"1 Chronicles 9:41","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":9,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":9,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>and Ahaz Added from 1 Chronicles 8:35.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-11-5","title":"1 Chronicles 11:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>castle of Zion Heb. castle. (1) Zion, the ancient Jebusite stronghold, is the southwest eminence in Jerusalem, called in Scripture the city of David, and associated with the Davidic royalty both historically and prophetically 1 Chronicles 11:7; Psalms 2:6; Isaiah 2:3. The word is often used of the whole city of Jerusalem considered as the city of God Psalms 48:2,3 especially in passages referring to the future kingdom-age ; Isaiah 1:27; 2:3; 4:1-6; Joel 3:16; Zechariah 1:16,17; 8:3-8; Romans 11:26. In Hebrews 12:22 the word is used symbolically of heaven. (2) In Deuteronomy 4:48 the name is given to a projection or peak of Mount Hermon.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-12-15","title":"1 Chronicles 12:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":12,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":12,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>first month i.e. April.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-13-11","title":"1 Chronicles 13:11","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":13,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":13,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Perezuzza i.e. the breach of Uzza.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-16-4","title":"1 Chronicles 16:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>record See titles of Psalms 38 and 70.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-16-16","title":"1 Chronicles 16:16","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>Abraham (See Scofield \"Genesis 15:18\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-16-25","title":"1 Chronicles 16:25","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>feared (See Scofield \"Psalms 19:9\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-16-37","title":"1 Chronicles 16:37","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":16,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":16,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>It will be understood that the ancient tabernacle was now divided; the ark was brought into \"Zion.\" (See Scofield \"1 Chronicles 11:5\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-18-8","title":"1 Chronicles 18:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Tibhath Called Betah, and Berothai. 2 Samuel 8:8.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-18-12","title":"1 Chronicles 18:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":18,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":18,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Abishai Nephew of David, brother to Joab. 2 Samuel 23:18; 1 Chronicles 2:16.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-20-1","title":"1 Chronicles 20:1","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>David Here should be read 2 Samuel 11:2-12:25; Psalms 51:1-19.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-21-4","title":"1 Chronicles 21:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>departed Here should read 2 Samuel 24:4-9.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-21-5","title":"1 Chronicles 21:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>were a thousand Cf. (See Scofield \"2 Samuel 24:9\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-21-12","title":"1 Chronicles 21:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Marg (See Scofield \"Hebrews 1:4\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-21-15","title":"1 Chronicles 21:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>angel (See Scofield \"Hebrews 1:4\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-21-18","title":"1 Chronicles 21:18","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>angel (See Scofield \"Hebrews 1:4\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-21-20","title":"1 Chronicles 21:20","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>angel (See Scofield \"Hebrews 1:4\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-21-25","title":"1 Chronicles 21:25","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>six hundred shekels of gold A discrepancy has been imagined in the two accounts, 2 Samuel 24:24,; 1 Chronicles 21:25; 2 Samuel 24:24 records the price of the threshingfloor (heb. goren); 1 Chronicles 21:25 of the place (Heb. magom, lit. \"home,\" 1 Samuel 2:20) same word or area on which afterward the great temple, with its spacious courts was built. 2 Chronicles 3:1. David gave fifty shekels of sliver for the \"goren\"; six hundred shekels of gold for the \"magom.\"</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-21-27","title":"1 Chronicles 21:27","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":21,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":21,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>angel (See Scofield \"Hebrews 1:4\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-23-22","title":"1 Chronicles 23:22","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>brethren i.e. cousins.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-23-28","title":"1 Chronicles 23:28","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>office i.e. their new office, since their former office of bearing the tabernacle was ended.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-23-29","title":"1 Chronicles 23:29","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":23,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":23,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>shewbread (See Scofield \"Exodus 25:30\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-2","title":"1 Chronicles 27:2","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>first month i.e. April; 1 Chronicles 27:3.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-4","title":"1 Chronicles 27:4","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>second month i.e. May.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-5","title":"1 Chronicles 27:5","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>third month i.e. June.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-7","title":"1 Chronicles 27:7","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>fourth month i.e. July.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-8","title":"1 Chronicles 27:8","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>fifth month i.e. August.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-9","title":"1 Chronicles 27:9","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>sixth month i.e. September.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-10","title":"1 Chronicles 27:10","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>seventh month i.e. October.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-11","title":"1 Chronicles 27:11","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>eighth month i.e. November.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-12","title":"1 Chronicles 27:12","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>ninth month i.e. December.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-13","title":"1 Chronicles 27:13","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>tenth month i.e. January.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-14","title":"1 Chronicles 27:14","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>eleventh month i.e. February.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-27-15","title":"1 Chronicles 27:15","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":27,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":27,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>twelfth month i.e. March.</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-28-16","title":"1 Chronicles 28:16","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":28,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":28,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>shewbread (See Scofield \"Exodus 25:30\") .</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-29-10","title":"1 Chronicles 29:10","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>blessed Note the order: 1 Chronicles 29:3-8, giving, 1 Chronicles 29:9, joy, 1 Chronicles 29:10, blessing, 1 Chronicles 29:11-19, prayer, 1 Chronicles 29:20, worship:</p>"},{"id":"scofield-1ch-29-29","title":"1 Chronicles 29:29","author":"C. I. Scofield (1843–1921)","reference":{"book":"1CH","chapterStart":29,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":29,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>book of These books have perished.</p>"}]}